        "type": "4-Mark Inference",
        "marks": 4,
        "targetMins": 5,
        "questionText": "Give two things you can infer from Source A about the dangers faced by civil rights volunteers during the Freedom Summer in Mississippi in 1964.",
        "stimulus": [],
        "sourceExtract": "<div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\">Source A: From a diary entry written by a white college student volunteering in Mississippi, July 1964.</div><div>We are told never to stand near windows at night and to always check our cars before starting the engines. Everyone is terrified after the disappearance of the three boys, but seeing the courage of the local black families who still show up to our Freedom Schools makes me determined not to leave.</div>",
        "modelAnswer": "<strong>Sample Acceptable Inferences (the dangers faced by civil rights volunteers during the Freedom Summer in Mississippi in 1964):</strong>\n• <strong>Inference 1:</strong> Civil rights volunteers lived in constant terror of violent white supremacist attacks.<br>&bull; <em>Detail from source:</em> \"We are told never to stand near windows at night and to always check our cars before starting the engines. Everyone is terrified after the disappearance of the three boys...\"\n\n• <strong>Inference 2:</strong> The commitment of local Black families encouraged volunteers to persevere despite lethal risks.<br>&bull; <em>Detail from source:</em> \"seeing the courage of the local black families who still show up to our Freedom Schools makes me determined not to leave.\"",
