        "sourceExtract": "<div style=\"font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 600;\">Source A: From an official report by a US military liaison in Saigon, 1962.</div><div>The fortified hamlets are secured with barbed wire and trenches, which deters insurgent entry but alienates the rural population. Peasants resent being relocated from their traditional lands. Consequently, many villagers secretly cooperate with the Vietcong due to their hostility toward the resettlement program.</div>",
        "modelAnswer": "<strong>Sample Acceptable Inferences (the Strategic Hamlet Program in South Vietnam in 1962):</strong>\n• <strong>Inference 1:</strong> The forced relocation of rural peasants caused widespread resentment against the South Vietnamese government.<br>&bull; <em>Detail from source:</em> \"alienates the rural population. Peasants resent being relocated from their traditional lands.\"\n\n• <strong>Inference 2:</strong> The program backfired by driving hostile villagers into secretly supporting the Vietcong.<br>&bull; <em>Detail from source:</em> \"Consequently, many villagers secretly cooperate with the Vietcong due to their hostility toward the resettlement program.\"",
        "pdfUrl": "/pdfs/mocks/usa/usa_mock_5_question_booklet.pdf",
